Subject: gfx_pc: the VR mode's eye matrix, substituted at 0030's two MP sites (VR R0)

VR round R0 (docs/VR-CHARTER.md §5, §4 D2; docs/VR-R0-FINDINGS.md; D-100).
Stacked on 0030's inserted gfx_stereo_projection() text, which works in this
repo exactly as 0033/0034/0055 already do (D-101: the charter's "0030
regenerations through its generator" is a Shipwright inheritance; there is no
generator here and no reverse probe).

While pdVisionVRActive() is 1 - the VR compositor loop is running in world
mode with a published eye law - gfx_stereo_projection() hands the projection
to gfx_vr_projection() instead of folding an offset into it:

  * FLAT (menuRender's span, 0032) keeps the game's own matrix, exactly as the
    3D path does;
  * every other projection is decomposed exactly as View * Pg (Pg a plain
    guPerspectiveF, View the identity for props, the baked camera for the bg,
    the camera's rotation for the sky) and rebuilt as View * E' * P_eye, where
    E is the shell's head-to-eye transform (A.V, PD units, row-vector), E' is
    E with its translation scaled by bg_scale for a baked matrix and dropped for
    the SKY, and P_eye is the compositor's asymmetric frustum with the class's
    OWN depth row (so the world, the sky and the gun keep their ranges);
  * a plain WORLD load is E * P_eye exactly, which is what the shell publishes
    as EyeVP, and the engine reports what it substituted (`vr pose`);
  * 0034's near law stays disarmed (near_k is cleared before the gate).

When the gate is 0 - 2D, the 3D panel mode, and every non-visionOS build -
nothing after it has changed: the 3D fold is byte-for-byte the same path, and
off visionOS none of this compiles (PD_VISION_STEREO is 0). The 2D seeded
replay against the macOS oracle is the proof.

